# PH: hand the cards back to production. This is the LAST job of the window and it runs even when a stop job (PA0 or P2) halted the window
# and after a stall, a hang or a cancelled gate, any of which can leave all four cards hung with production down: the status of every
# board and the all-four reset. The driver then runs, OUTSIDE this job file: the platform's fabric re-measure (links train only at board
# init, and production needs two links per pair); the agentstart action (start the node agent again; it waits for its container to answer
# /v1/models); then production is placed again by the OWNER's /deploy of today's production recipe (the thin layer image the rig daemon's
# :latest already names; profile c2-packed-tp4, verify audits OFF, QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1), which needs the owner's go-ahead
# and an admin token. This template never deploys anything.
# NEVER place a gate arm: not c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace, not the tp4-prof-2 image. Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the
# fabric re-measure passes, the endpoint answers /v1/models with the production model and a chat completes, and the engine log shows
# profile c2-packed-tp4 with the audits off. If the reset does not heal a board after a stall, production stays down until it does.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-3-prof window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-prof and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a
# card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (it is the last job).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prof-2
